  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Mass of Urea <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CONH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> required to be dissolved in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;of water in order to reduce the vapour pressure of water by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_______</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>.</mo></math> (Nearest integer)</p><p>Given : Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>16</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p>",
